==Wyrmscraig==
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (1).png|thumb|center|600px|You can find Wyrmscraig South-West of Charred Island.]]
Wyrmscraig is a brand-new island, made with community member <u>[https://x.com/ScreteMonge Gnome]</u>... Or, RoseNMcGeet as he also likes to be called. You may also know him as ScreteMonge, the man has three names! 

You may know of Gnome through his work on RuneLite's creator toolkit plug-in, or some of his collaboration with some popular community suggestions floating around on our subreddit!

It's been a pleasure to work with Gnome on his fantastic concept and bring to life in-game. A huge thanks to Gnome is deserved, as well as you, our wonderful community, for your feedback and thoughts throughout the process of development.

To every single of you who entered the Player-Designed Island competition when we ran it back in December: thank you. Thousands of you poured your passion (and a few memes) into your entries. Whilst we couldn't pick multiple entries for this project, your ideas have given the team many new avenues for future exploration. Seeing what kinds of ideas you are interested in is a fantastic tool for developers like us, and helps us understand what kind of content you're interested in next. 

Wyrmscraig is proof of what happens when player creativity meets the sandbox that is Old School RuneScape. We are so excited to see what you think, and how our community will continue to shape future content, inspiring us, and uplifting us with all of your suggestions and ideas.

So, what are you waiting for? To get started with this content, you'll need 62 Sailing.

While you can start exploring the island right away, and even participate in some of the activities (like Goat Hunting), you might want to get started by completing ''Fallen From Grace.'' 

==Fallen From Grace==
Fallen from Grace is an Experienced, Short length quest.

Your adventure will begin in the village of Auchrie, where a disappearance has left the locals fearful and suspicious of outsiders. With one of their own still missing, they'll reluctantly turn to you for help.

As you explore the island, you'll uncover ancient secrets, investigate the mystery of the Mad Angel, and discover the truth behind the disappearances haunting the island.

====Requirements====
To start the quest you'll need '''62 Sailing, 60 Crafting, 47 Runecraft, and 53 Mining.''' Just speak to Cormac, located in the middle of the Auchrie village.

[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (2).png|center|319px]]


[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (3).png|center|300px]]

====Rewards====

* 10,000 Crafting
* 12,500 Sailing
* 5,000 Mining
* 5,000 Runecraft XP
* Access to the repeatable boss encounter
* Access to Sunstone Golem Crafting & Mining
* Teleports
** Slayer Ring: Teleport to Wyrmscraig's cavern.
** Necklace of Passage: Teleport to Wyrmscraig, south of Sunstone mine.

==Repeatable Mad Angel Boss==
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (4).png|center|600px]]

Once you've completed ''Fallen From Grace,'' you'll be able to return to the Cathedral and challenge the repeatable version of the boss you first encountered during the quest.

Designed as a mid-level PvM encounter, it's a great next step for players who have already earned their Fire Cape and are looking to take on a rewarding new challenge.

During development, it was our intention to ensure that the quest version of the boss was identical to the repeatable version. However, when it came to playtesting, we made some tweaks to tone her down a little for the quest. This is because we want to ensure that the fight matches the difficulty of other quests in the same tier. 

===Unique Reward: Hallowfell===
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (5).gif|center|350px]]

Defeating the boss gives you the chance to earn a range of unique rewards, including Hallowfell, a powerful two-handed sword that requires '''75 Attack''' to wield.

[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (6).png|center|400px]]

Every swing cleaves through nearby enemies, hitting up to two additional targets. Against three monsters it actually outperforms every other melee weapon currently available, making it a very juicy upgrade for all different types of accounts.

The repeatable boss also drops the following:

* Boss Teleport Scrolls: Provides a direct teleport back to the encounter.
* Granite Dust
** ''Please note, this isn't expected to drop in large quantities, it's just an additional source which felt thematically appropriate.''
* Boss Jar
* New Pet

[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (7).gif|center|450px]]

==New Slayer Master: Mortimer==
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (8).png|center|600px]]

Mortimer is a new, high-level Slayer Master built around player choice.

From a design perspective, our main goal is to offer a unique twist on Slayer with  his modifiers, and to provide a different experience by boosting some typically less desirable tasks. Unlocking him should be a meaningful boost over existing methods.

Instead of assigning you a single Slayer task, Mortimer gives you a choice between two assignments. As you prove yourself by completing tasks for him, you'll eventually unlock a third choice, giving you even greater flexibility when deciding what to tackle next.

You unlock Mortimer with 100 Combat and 70 Slayer, or 99 Slayer, regardless of your Combat level.

We've covered Mortimer in <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/meet-mortimer-your-newest-slayer-master?oldschool=1 our recent blog]</u>, but here's the TLDR:

* His task list features creatures with Superior variants only.
* Tasks assigned by Mortimer are significantly more expensive to skip (100 Slayer points), and cannot be reset through Turael.
* While using Mortimer you'll only have access to '''two block slots''', each costing '''120 Slayer Points'''. Meaning, if you receive a task you'd rather not complete, your options are to skip it, store it or finish it before taking on any other Slayer assignment.
* He doesn't offer Slayer Points for his tasks (unless you have the Points Mortifier active).
* As you continue completing tasks for Mortimer, you'll begin unlocking additional bonuses: Mortifiers. These are powerful effects that may occasionally appear alongside your task choices, offering extra rewards or benefits depending on the assignment you choose.

===Mortifiers===
Based on feedback last week, we've reduced the required tasks required to unlock modifiers by around half.

Here are the new tasks required to unlock each Mortifier:

