==Goat Hunting==
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (10).png|center|600px]]

Goat Hunting is a brand-new Hunter training activity found on Wyrmscraig. You'll herd the island's concerning goat population into a deadly pit!

This activity offers an active and engaging alternative to Red and Black Salamanders at 60 - 80 Hunter.

====Requirements====
To access Goat Hunting, you'll need:


* 60 Hunter
* Completion of Sheep Herder

===Gameplay===

* Herd goats
** Construct a pit with the nearby resources on the island to lure goats to their doom.
** You'll need to encourage goats into this deadly pit using a cattleprod, granting Hunter XP once inside.
** You can also choose to use Telekinetic Grab or Dark Lure if preferred, giving Magic a little bit of extra utility.
* Make sure the pit is full
** The number of goats required to fill the pit scales based on your Hunter level.
* Process XP and materials
** For each goat successfully herded into the pit, you'll receive a small amount of Hunter XP immediately.
** The majority of the XP comes afterwards when interacting with the pit itself and processing the goats collected inside.
* Re-arm the pit with a new spike set and repeat.

===Rewards===
The focus of this activity is primarily on Hunter XP, which should sit between Red and Black Salamanders. However, drops include Goat Horns (useful for Combat Potions) and Goat Fur (to be used within Golem Crafting if desired).

The activity also drops a pet, Mr McGroot.

For those of you curious about drop rates, hang on in there. We'll reveal the details on drop rates roughly 2 weeks from now! 

==Sunstone Mining & Golem Crafting==
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (11).png|center|600px]]

Once you have completed Fallen From Grace, you'll learn about Golem Crafting, a new Crafting training method. This is intended to be a viable alternative to Glassblowing, especially at higher levels.

To access Sunstone Golem Crafting, you'll need:

* Level 60 Crafting
* Completion of ''Fallen from Grace ''

During this activity, you will mine an inventory of Sunstone, sculpt Golems and clothe them with furs from Hunter. Remember, this activity requires Hunter Furs, so bring them along with you, along with your Chisel and Hammer.

As a reminder, the shop stock for Moonlight Antelope Fur has been reduced to 0. You can still trade Furs with other players, it's just not buyable in shops anymore. 

Golem Crafting can be a relaxed, or higher intensity training method depending on your preferred playstyle. 

===Gameplay===
The gameplay loop is very simple and similar to Vale Totems, if you're familiar with this activity from Varlamore.  

====Sunstone Mining====
You'll find sunstone rocks on Wyrmscraig. You can click them, mine them, get the resource, and then it depletes. You need''' 53 Mining '''for Sunstone.

Momentum is a brand-new mechanic for mining Sunstone. This is a static bonus earned by continuously mining. As your momentum builds, you'll mine more efficiently, getting additional Sunstone ore, and bonus Mining XP. Losing your Momentum resets the benefits, which should encourage active mining for those who want to play more efficiently. At '''80 Mining, '''you'll see guaranteed success from the momentum mechanic.

It's worth mentioning that during this activity, you benefit from any upgrades that enhance Mining, such as Expert Mining Gloves.

For a more relaxed approach, you can click on the nearby Sunstone Monolith to gather Sunstone instead. This will be slower, but more AFK!

====Golem Crafting====
Head over to the Golem Crafting stations nearby with your Sunstone, Chisel, Hammer and Fur. 

[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (12).png|center|450px]]

* Shape the Golem
** Using a Chisel and with Sunstone in your inventory, work on the Golem from each of its four sides: North, East, South, and West. Completing all four sides earns small amounts of Crafting XP.
* Create a Sunstone Core
** Use a Chisel on a piece of Sunstone to create a Sunstone Core. This requires 60 Crafting and can be done in advance, so you can prepare several of them before heading to the activity.
* Insert the Sunstone Core
** Once all four sides have been shaped, just insert the Sunstone Core to complete the Golem.
* Clothe Golems in Hunter Furs
** All Hunter Furs have the same Crafting requirement (60) and use 1 Fur.

===Rewards===
====Jeweller's Chisel====
You can earn the Jeweller's Chisel from Golem Crafting. It offers the following benefits: 

* A 20% increased chance to successfully cut Opals, Jades and Topaz.
* A 10% chance to cut two gems at once when cutting any gem.
* Guaranteed success when cutting:
** Opals at Level 62.
** Jades at Level 71.
** Topaz at Level 76.

Mod Ed has also managed to ensure that the Jeweller's Chisel also functions as a regular chisel, too, so you won't need to carry two around with you in Gielinor. Bang!

Lastly, we mentioned in our previous blog that you can obtain stardust in small quantities from this activity. This has been changed during our system reviews. Instead, the loot table now offers Uncut Sapphire, Emeralds, Rubies and Diamonds.

===Other Sailing Changes===
[[File:Wyrmscraig Is Out Today! (13).png|center|476px]]

* Added the 'Teleport to Boat' spell as an additional Sailing Skillcape perk. The Greater Teleport Focus facility is still required to use it.

